---
// PODDEN OCH APPEN — what the site offers besides the page, in the closing promotion region beside the book.
//
// The podcast is "a big thing" the front page had missed (user review, 2026-09-25), so it
// got a movement of its own here: the show's cover, a paragraph, and the three newest
// episodes with a play control each. In review that movement felt misplaced — a second
// list of essays, in a vocabulary the rest of the page does not use, and one more
// screen of text between the cover's photograph and the next picture. What was wanted
// was the podcast PROMOTED, not the essays played on the front page ("det hade räckt …
// att bara promota podden", 2026-09-26), and the app beside it.
//
// So: two halves, each a drawing, a kicker, one line and the ways in (Promo.astro, the
// grammar the book and the mosque screen share). The drawings
// (src/assets/ritningar; how they were made is in its README) replaced the products'
// own faces, the podcast cover and the app icon (2026-09-26): at 7rem those read as two
// logos, a blue tile and a printed square in fixed colours on a band otherwise all ink
// and paper. One-ink line drawings came next and were "too simple"; then a worked
// pencil drawing after a Carl Larsson reference; the user then pointed to a page of
// J. M. W. Turner's sketchbook, and to the app's own screenshots. So: graphite in the
// manner of Turner's studies — quick, searching lines, open paper — with one ochre
// pencil for what is gold in the app: headphones on an open book with its ribbon, and a
// phone showing the app itself, the map with the day's arc and the list of the prayers
// with the current one lit. Each is drawn twice: graphite on white paper for the light
// theme, and the same pair in white chalk on black paper for the dark — Turner's own
// practice on toned paper, and the only honest translation: a tonal drawing inverted
// turns negative (the dark screen went white, the shadows glowed), and a light sheet of
// paper laid on the dark band "doesn't work" (user review, 2026-09-26). <Ritning> draws
// them, as it draws the series' other drawings across the site.
import { APP_STORE_URL, PLAY_STORE_URL } from "../lib/app";
import { getArticles } from "../lib/articles";
import { RITNINGAR } from "../lib/ritningar";
import PodcastBrandIcon from "./PodcastBrandIcon.astro";
import PodcastSubscribeLinks from "./PodcastSubscribeLinks.astro";
import Promo from "./Promo.astro";

const articles = await getArticles();
// One size for every mark in the band's five pills; 14px, the pill default, read as
// specks beside sentence-case labels.
const ICON = 18;
const narrated = articles.filter((a) => typeof a.audioFile === "string");
---

{
	narrated.length > 0 && (
		<Promo id="podden-rubrik" kicker="Podd" titel="Essäerna, inlästa" href="/podcast/" ritning={RITNINGAR.podden}>
			Lyssna på essäerna i Apple Podcasts, Spotify eller en annan poddspelare.
			<PodcastSubscribeLinks slot="lankar" actionClass="pill" iconSize={ICON} />
		</Promo>
	)
}

<Promo id="appen-rubrik" kicker="App" titel="Bönetiderna i mobilen" href="/app/" ritning={RITNINGAR.appen}>
	En påminnelse före varje bön och en kompass mot Kaba. Gratis och utan annonser.
	<Fragment slot="lankar">
		<a class="pill" href={APP_STORE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
			<PodcastBrandIcon platform="appstore" size={ICON} />
			App Store
		</a>
		<a class="pill" href={PLAY_STORE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
			<PodcastBrandIcon platform="googleplay" size={ICON} />
			Google Play
		</a>
	</Fragment>
</Promo>
